  "question": {
    "text": "Consider a plane <math><mi>P</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>,&nbsp;a line <math><mi>L</mi><mo>:</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> and a point <math><mi>A</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4,1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. If the line <math><mi>L</mi></math> intersects plane <math><mi>P</mi></math> at <math><mi>B</mi></math> and the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></math> plane at <math><mi>C</mi></math>, then the area (in sq. units) of <math><mo>∆</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
